WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.306 --> 00:00:15.267
Zann's hand flew to his forehead.

2
00:00:15.747 --> 00:00:17.088
The purple marks were gone!

3
00:00:18.148 --> 00:00:21.850
"Maybe we can get them back with a Restore spell," Perda suggested.

4
00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:25.692
"But we haven't learned those yet," protested Gliss.

5
00:00:25.712 --> 00:00:27.273
"So what?

6
00:00:27.753 --> 00:00:28.794
It's worth a try."

7
00:00:29.614 --> 00:00:30.955
Perda rubbed her hands together.

8
00:00:30.975 --> 00:00:34.813
"Restore!" Zann stared at her hopefully.

9
00:00:34.833 --> 00:00:37.594
"Well?" "Nothing."

10
00:00:37.875 --> 00:00:39.255
Perda's shoulders slumped.

11
00:00:39.796 --> 00:00:40.776
"Sorry, guys."

12
00:00:41.737 --> 00:00:42.897
Darb shaded his eyes.

13
00:00:42.917 --> 00:00:44.458
"Look, someone's coming."

14
00:00:45.379 --> 00:00:46.739
A woman was walking toward them.

15
00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:51.522
She was blue-skinned and bald, with a pretty, smiling face.

16
00:00:51.542 --> 00:00:53.763
"Hello," she greeted them.

17
00:00:54.344 --> 00:00:55.384
"My name is Vee.

18
00:00:55.945 --> 00:00:57.826
I am the guardian of the wormhole."

19
00:00:57.846 --> 00:01:01.047
"Why does this wormhole need a guardian?"

20
00:01:01.328 --> 00:01:01.968
Perda asked.

21
00:01:02.808 --> 00:01:05.330
"We've had some trouble lately," Vee replied.

22
00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:07.351
"What kind of trouble?"

23
00:01:07.672 --> 00:01:08.212
said Gliss.

24
00:01:08.232 --> 00:01:10.674
"The details aren't important."

25
00:01:11.054 --> 00:01:12.155
Vee was still smiling.

26
00:01:12.175 --> 00:01:15.117
"What brings you young people to Pax?"

27
00:01:15.137 --> 00:01:18.920
"Pax? Is that the name of this world?"

28
00:01:19.901 --> 00:01:23.343
Zann didn't remember ever hearing his parents mention a world by that name.

29
00:01:24.264 --> 00:01:25.945
Perda didn't seem to recognize it either.

30
00:01:26.806 --> 00:01:29.448
That meant it probably wasn't in any of his parents' books.

31
00:01:30.328 --> 00:01:32.730
"We're looking for two people," Gliss said.

32
00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:36.934
"A woman named Wyssa and a man named Morb."

33
00:01:38.035 --> 00:01:41.318
Vee gasped, her pleasant expression turning fearful.

34
00:01:42.318 --> 00:01:44.560
"Why are you looking for Morb?

35
00:01:45.321 --> 00:01:46.582
Are you friends of his?"

36
00:01:46.602 --> 00:01:48.884
"No way!"

37
00:01:49.124 --> 00:01:49.905
Perda exclaimed.

38
00:01:49.925 --> 00:01:51.386
"Morb is evil."

39
00:01:52.427 --> 00:01:53.388
Vee looked relieved.

40
00:01:53.408 --> 00:01:54.809
"Yes, we know.

41
00:01:55.410 --> 00:01:57.832
He's the reason I was sent to guard the wormhole."

42
00:01:58.768 --> 00:02:00.129
"So he was here recently?"

43
00:02:00.370 --> 00:02:00.950
Zann asked.

44
00:02:01.811 --> 00:02:02.411
Vee nodded.

45
00:02:02.431 --> 00:02:06.515
"He visited Pax just long enough to steal a mibbit."

46
00:02:06.535 --> 00:02:08.236
"A mibbit?”

47
00:02:08.496 --> 00:02:08.997
said Darb.

48
00:02:09.017 --> 00:02:09.878
"What's that?"

49
00:02:09.898 --> 00:02:14.201
"One of our most cherished creatures," Vee said.

50
00:02:14.221 --> 00:02:20.286
"Mibbits have very strong and specific magic, and they're prone to panic.

51
00:02:21.227 --> 00:02:26.612
When they panic, they send out powerful energy that overwhelms anyone nearby.

52
00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:31.762
Victims are unable to think or act or even move."

53
00:02:32.923 --> 00:02:35.564
Zann and the others exchanged concerned glances.

54
00:02:35.584 --> 00:02:39.567
"Uh-oh, that doesn't sound good," Perda said.

55
00:02:39.587 --> 00:02:44.629
"I bet Morb wants the mibbit to help him try to take over Magica again."

56
00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:46.930
Vee looked confused.

57
00:02:47.171 --> 00:02:48.431
"What are you talking about?"

58
00:02:49.412 --> 00:02:51.293
Zann quickly told her the whole story.

59
00:02:51.313 --> 00:02:56.996
"So that's why we're afraid that Morb might be gathering power again," he finished.

60
00:02:58.096 --> 00:03:01.159
"Maybe Morb is trying to force my parents to help him."

61
00:03:02.079 --> 00:03:06.623
"Then again, maybe Morb isn't interested in Magica anymore," Darb suggested.

62
00:03:06.643 --> 00:03:10.226
"Your parents know a lot about other worlds, right?

63
00:03:10.867 --> 00:03:15.330
Maybe Morb is planning to use their knowledge to take over a different world this time."

64
00:03:16.171 --> 00:03:17.552
"Like this one, maybe?"

65
00:03:17.932 --> 00:03:20.134
Gliss glanced around at the beautiful scenery.

66
00:03:20.154 --> 00:03:22.656
"It's really nice here.

67
00:03:23.176 --> 00:03:27.300
And Morb knows the mibbit's magic would definitely work on the people of Pax."

68
00:03:28.448 --> 00:03:32.172
"Or maybe he wants to take over World X," Zann said.

69
00:03:32.192 --> 00:03:35.415
"That could be why he's after my parents.

70
00:03:35.916 --> 00:03:37.377
He wants them to lead him there!"

71
00:03:37.397 --> 00:03:40.200
"That makes sense," Perda agreed.

72
00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:47.307
"If it's true that World X is some kind of gateway to all other worlds, controlling World X

73
00:03:47.667 --> 00:03:49.809
could give Morb incredible power."

74
00:03:50.850 --> 00:03:52.232
"Oh dear," Vee said.

75
00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:58.165
"I fear the powers of our sweet mibbit could help Morb take over any world."

76
00:03:59.566 --> 00:04:01.668
"How did he capture it, if it's that powerful?"

77
00:04:01.808 --> 00:04:02.409
Darb asked.

78
00:04:03.290 --> 00:04:04.210
Vee looked nervous.

79
00:04:04.230 --> 00:04:05.311
"We don't know.

80
00:04:06.252 --> 00:04:10.656
It would take unimaginable power to immobilize a mibbit without panicking it."

81
00:04:10.676 --> 00:04:14.800
"We really need to catch up to Wyssa now," Perda said.

82
00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:17.302
"We have to warn her about this!"

83
00:04:17.322 --> 00:04:19.004
"You're right.

84
00:04:19.636 --> 00:04:24.278
I don't think she realizes just how much power Morb must have now," Zann said.

85
00:04:24.298 --> 00:04:27.139
"Plus she doesn't know about the mibbit."

86
00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:29.821
"But how will we find Wyssa?"

87
00:04:30.061 --> 00:04:30.641
Gliss asked.

88
00:04:30.661 --> 00:04:33.822
"We've lost our only way of tracking her."

89
00:04:34.723 --> 00:04:35.763
Zann turned to Vee.

90
00:04:35.783 --> 00:04:39.885
"Do you know of any magic that could help us track someone through the vortex?"

91
00:04:39.905 --> 00:04:42.546
"I'm afraid not," Vee said.

92
00:04:42.566 --> 00:04:46.688
"Paxian magic is quite different from that of many other worlds.

93
00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:51.982
It mostly involves feelings and communications, not physical abilities."

94
00:04:52.002 --> 00:04:57.324
"Really? But you guys must be able to do the basic stuff, right?"

95
00:04:57.444 --> 00:04:58.105
Perda asked.

96
00:04:58.985 --> 00:05:03.547
"Like conjuring food, performing Blast spells, or building houses by magic?"

97
00:05:04.667 --> 00:05:06.648
"No, we can't do any of that."

98
00:05:07.068 --> 00:05:07.809
Vee sighed.

99
00:05:07.829 --> 00:05:13.771
"That's why Morb was able to overpower us so easily and steal the mibbit."

100
00:05:14.672 --> 00:05:20.183
"Wow." Zann glanced at the distant city on the hill, awed to think that it had been built

101
00:05:20.283 --> 00:05:21.904
entirely without magic.

102
00:05:23.445 --> 00:05:25.286
"That reminds me," Vee went on.

103
00:05:25.307 --> 00:05:29.549
"I should let my people know what you've just told me about Morb.

104
00:05:30.290 --> 00:05:32.331
Pardon me while I send them a mind message."

105
00:05:32.351 --> 00:05:34.433
"A mind message?"

106
00:05:34.693 --> 00:05:35.373
Gliss echoed.

107
00:05:35.393 --> 00:05:38.595
"It's a kind of telepathy," Vee explained.

108
00:05:38.615 --> 00:05:42.958
"We can all communicate within our minds anytime we wish."

109
00:05:42.978 --> 00:05:45.380
"Cool," Zann said.

110
00:05:45.784 --> 00:05:47.245
"Too bad we can't do that!"

111
00:05:48.065 --> 00:05:48.866
Perda smiled.

112
00:05:48.886 --> 00:05:54.129
"Yeah. It would save a lot of time, not having to inscribe message moths."

113
00:05:55.129 --> 00:05:56.350
Vee closed her eyes.

114
00:05:56.370 --> 00:06:03.214
"I'll just be a moment While Zann waited, he pulled out his message stone and stared at it

115
00:06:03.274 --> 00:06:07.196
helplessly. How could he find his parents before Morb did?

116
00:06:07.216 --> 00:06:08.517
"What's that?"

117
00:06:08.817 --> 00:06:10.438
Vee asked when she opened her eyes.

118
00:06:11.599 --> 00:06:13.420
Zann explained about message stones.

119
00:06:13.908 --> 00:06:16.949
"This one holds a message from my parents," he finished.

120
00:06:16.969 --> 00:06:19.931
"Too bad it can't tell us where they are now."

121
00:06:20.951 --> 00:06:21.711
Vee smiled.

122
00:06:22.111 --> 00:06:23.192
"Perhaps I can help.

123
00:06:24.112 --> 00:06:28.154
All objects hold psychic traces of the people who last held them.

124
00:06:29.014 --> 00:06:32.616
I might be able to read your stone—if you want me to."

125
00:06:32.636 --> 00:06:35.357
"Really? That would be great!"

126
00:06:35.757 --> 00:06:37.118
Zann handed her the stone.

127
00:06:38.578 --> 00:06:40.379
Vee took it and closed her eyes.

128
00:06:40.399 --> 00:06:47.664
"The vision is faint, but I see two people: a man and a woman She quickly described them.

129
00:06:47.684 --> 00:06:49.285
"That's them!"

130
00:06:49.626 --> 00:06:50.206
Zann cried.

131
00:06:50.226 --> 00:06:51.407
"My parents!

132
00:06:51.928 --> 00:06:52.889
What else can you see?"

133
00:06:53.769 --> 00:06:55.571
"They're in a forest," Vee said.

134
00:06:55.591 --> 00:07:01.576
"They're surrounded by tiny people—the people don't even come up to your parents' knees."

135
00:07:02.817 --> 00:07:03.638
Zann gasped.

136
00:07:03.658 --> 00:07:04.899
"World X!

137
00:07:05.499 --> 00:07:09.343
I knew it—my parents must be in World X!"
